      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, taking extra strength aspirin is likely unsafe for you since many post-surgery patients take blood thinners or other medications that increase bleeding risk, and aspirin can also irritate the stomach. Stick to taking the leftover ibuprofen only if your surgeon previously approved using it on your specific case and you haven't been told to avoid NSAIDs. Please prioritize firm elevation and icing over additional medication to manage the swelling this evening. If the redness spreads or you notice the calf becoming significantly colder or numb, seek urgent medical help before morning.",
